🎯 𝗞𝘂𝗯𝗲𝗿𝗻𝗲𝘁𝗲𝘀 𝗗𝗲𝗽𝗹𝗼𝘆𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁 𝗶𝘀 𝗨𝗻𝗮𝘃𝗮𝗶𝗹𝗮𝗯𝗹𝗲 — 𝗛𝗼𝘄 𝗪𝗼𝘂𝗹𝗱 𝗬𝗼𝘂 𝗧𝗿𝗼𝘂𝗯𝗹𝗲𝘀𝗵𝗼𝗼𝘁 𝗜𝘁?

𝗜𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗶𝗲𝘄 𝗤𝘂𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻:

You deployed a new application version to Kubernetes, but the Deployment is not becoming available. Users are experiencing downtime. How would you investigate and restore service in production?

Here’s my practical approach 👇

🔹 𝗦𝘁𝗲𝗽 𝟭: 𝗖𝗵𝗲𝗰𝗸 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗗𝗲𝗽𝗹𝗼𝘆𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁

kubectl get deployments -n <namespace>
kubectl describe deployment <deployment-name> -n <namespace>
kubectl rollout status deployment/<deployment-name> -n <namespace>

Check the desired replicas, available replicas, rollout status, and Events.

🔹 𝗦𝘁𝗲𝗽 𝟮: 𝗖𝗵𝗲𝗰𝗸 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗣𝗼𝗱𝘀

kubectl get pods -n <namespace> -o wide
kubectl get events -n <namespace> --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp

Look for "Pending", "CrashLoopBackOff", "ImagePullBackOff", failed scheduling, or readiness probe failures.

🔹 𝗦𝘁𝗲𝗽 𝟯: 𝗜𝗻𝘀𝗽𝗲𝗰𝘁 𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗹𝗶𝗰𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗟𝗼𝗴𝘀

kubectl logs <pod-name> -n <namespace> --all-containers=true
kubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n <namespace>

Identify startup errors, invalid configuration, dependency failures, and resource-related problems.

🔹 𝗦𝘁𝗲𝗽 𝟰: 𝗖𝗵𝗲𝗰𝗸 𝗥𝗼𝗹𝗹𝗼𝘂𝘁 𝗛𝗶𝘀𝘁𝗼𝗿𝘆

kubectl rollout history deployment/<deployment-name> -n <namespace>

Determine whether the latest ReplicaSet is failing to become available and whether the previous version was healthy.

🔹 𝗦𝘁𝗲𝗽 𝟱: 𝗥𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗼𝗿𝗲 𝗦𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗶𝗰𝗲 𝗶𝗳 𝗡𝗲𝗲𝗱𝗲𝗱

If the new release is causing an outage and the previous revision is known to be healthy, consider a controlled rollback:

kubectl rollout undo deployment/<deployment-name> -n <namespace>
kubectl rollout status deployment/<deployment-name> -n <namespace>

Follow your production change process and verify application health after rollback.

🔹 𝗦𝘁𝗲𝗽 𝟲: 𝗩𝗲𝗿𝗶𝗳𝘆 𝗥𝗲𝗰𝗼𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘆

kubectl get deployments,pods,svc -n <namespace>

Confirm the expected replicas are available, the Pods are Ready, and traffic is reaching the application.

💡 𝗞𝗲𝘆 𝗟𝗲𝗮𝗿𝗻𝗶𝗻𝗴:

In production, investigate first, restore service safely, and then identify the root cause.

A successful "kubectl apply" does not guarantee a successful deployment.
